== Detailed voting results<span class="anchor" id="Scoreboard"></span> ==
<!-- Anchor in the header is the old section name -->
The EBU introduced an undisclosed threshold number of [[Televoting|televotes]] that would have to be registered in each voting country in order to make that country's votes valid. If that number was not reached, the country's backup jury would vote instead. This affected Albania, Andorra and Monaco in the semi-final, and Andorra, Moldova and Monaco in the final.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bakker |first1=Sietse |title=Semifinal: No televoting in three countries |url=https://esctoday.com/4594/semifinal_no_televoting_in_three_countries/ |publisher=ESCToday |access-date=29 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151222091247/http://esctoday.com/4594/semifinal_no_televoting_in_three_countries/ |archive-date=22 December 2015 |date=20 May 2005 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Philips |first1=Roel |title=Moldovan Parliament doubts Moldovan votes |url=https://esctoday.com/4662/moldovan_parliament_doubts_moldovan_votes/ |publisher=ESCToday |access-date=29 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180402231247/http://esctoday.com/4662/moldovan_parliament_doubts_moldovan_votes/ |archive-date=2 April 2018 |date=1 June 2005 |url-status=live}}</ref>

