==Official album==
[[File:ESC 2005 album cover.jpg|thumb|right|Cover art of the official album]]
'''''Eurovision Song Contest: Kyiv 2005''''' was the official compilation album of the 2005 contest, put together by the European Broadcasting Union and released by [[EMI Records]] and [[CMC International]] on 2 May 2005. The album featured all 39 songs that entered in the 2005 contest, including the semi-finalists that failed to qualify into the grand final.<ref>{{cite web|author1=Sietse Bakker|title=Pre-order the official 2005 album and DVD|url=http://esctoday.com/3997/pre-order_the_official_2005_album_and_dvd/|website=esctoday.com|publisher=ESCToday|access-date=5 November 2014|date=9 March 2005|archive-date=5 November 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141105140117/http://esctoday.com/3997/pre-order_the_official_2005_album_and_dvd/|url-status=live}}</ref>

The original cover designed for the album was changed after {{Esccnty|Lebanon}}'s withdrawal from the Eurovision Song Contest 2005 after announcing they would show advertisements over the Israeli entry. Had they entered, they would have been on track 4, disc 2 with the song "[[Quand tout s'enfuit]]" by [[Aline Lahoud]].<ref>{{cite web|author1=Sietse Bakker|title=Lebanon withdraws|url=http://esctoday.com/4060/breaking_news_lebanon_withdraws/|website=esctoday.com|publisher=ESCToday|access-date=5 November 2014|date=18 March 2005|archive-date=30 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200930151758/http://esctoday.com/4060/breaking_news_lebanon_withdraws/|url-status=live}}</ref>

It was reported that sales of the 2005 Eurovision merchandise reached record-breaking levels.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Phillips|first1=Roel|title=Record sales of Eurovision merchandising|url=http://esctoday.com/4577/record_sales_of_eurovision_merchandising/|website=esctoday.com|publisher=ESCTOday|access-date=5 November 2014|date=19 May 2005|archive-date=5 November 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141105135741/http://esctoday.com/4577/record_sales_of_eurovision_merchandising/|url-status=live}}</ref>

